     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nIf 1,700 mg per dose is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it as written. I'd add a note on the order that you've confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
